eman.2", "P.Zoller.1", "A.S.Parkins.1", "O.Adetunji.1", "M.J.Collett.1", "J.Dalibard.1", "C.W.Gardiner.1"], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics"}], "author_count": 1, "first_author": {"full_name": "Wiseman, H.M.", "last_name": "Wiseman", "first_name": "H.M.", "recid": 1973243}, "control_number": 2948611, "dois": [{"source": "APS", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.49.2133"}], "earliest_date": "1994-03-01", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Wiseman:1994omv"], "abstracts": [{"source": "APS", "value": "A general theory of quantum-limited feedback for continuously monitored systems is presented. Two approaches are used, one based on quantum measurement theory and one on Hamiltonian system-bath interactions. The former gives rise to a stochastic non-Markovian evolution equation for the density operator, and the latter a non-Markovian quantum Langevin equation. In the limit that the time delay in the feedback loop is negligible, a simple deterministic Markovian master equation can be derived from either approach. Two special cases of interest are treated: feedback mediated by optical homodyne detection and self-excited quantum point processes.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "APS", "title": "Quantum theory of continuous feedback"}], "facet_author_name": ["1973243_Howard M. Wiseman"], "core": false, "imprints": [{"date": "1994-03-01"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2948611", "updated": "2025-07-18T11:25:22.614544"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.A", "Phys. Rev. A"]}, "id": "2948611", "updated": "2025-07-18T11:25:22.614544+00:00", "created": "2025-07-18T07:04:02.728040+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.49.2133&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.49.2133&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/ap